=== AI-OFF CONTRACT ===

I1  default-off:    PASS
    Evidence: migrations/000201_ai_settings.up.sql sets `DEFAULT 'off'`
    on the value_text column for ai_mode. defaultSettings() in
    internal/database/settings_repo.go returns AIMode='off',
    AIFeatures=map[string]bool{}, AIProviderConfig=map[string]any{},
    AICostCapCents=0. Every fresh install reads off mode.

I5  hidden UI:      PASS
    Evidence: web/src/ai/__tests__/offMode.invariant.test.tsx
    iterates AI_FEATURE_IDS, mounts each feature's Wrapped component
    with ai_mode='off' settings, and asserts no [data-ai-feature]
    element exists in the rendered tree. 2 tests pass; loop scales
    automatically to every future slice's registry entry.

I6  404 routes:     PASS
    Evidence: TestGuard_OffModeReturns404 in
    internal/ai/guard/off_mode_test.go drives an httptest router that
    constructs Guard.Wrap("chatbot-llm", handler) the same way
    mountAIRoutes does at boot, then asserts POST /api/v1/ai/chatbot
    returns 404 with ai_mode='off'. PASS.

I7  type system:    PASS
    Evidence: tools/aivet (Go AST analysis) returned EXIT=0 with
    "1 AI route(s), 1 feature(s) in registry, TS mirror in sync".
    The teslasync/ai-component-must-be-wrapped ESLint rule is
    registered in web/eslint.config.js and unit-tested in
    web/src/ai/__tests__/eslintRule.test.ts (7 tests pass) — a slice
    that ships an unwrapped AI surface fails CI before merge.

I9  no provider config leak in off mode: PASS
    Evidence: internal/api/settings_handler.go's Get handler sets
    `s.AIProviderConfig = nil` when AIMode='off' before serializing
    the response. The Update handler preserves the stored
    AIProviderConfig when the incoming body's field is nil so an
    off-mode SPA round-trip cannot wipe saved keys.

Methodology cross-references:
    P6 (type-system enforcement)        — guard.Wrap, withAiFeature, ESLint rule
    P9 (single-source-of-truth registry) — internal/ai/features.Registry
    D8 (404 not 403 in off mode)         — guard.Wrap implementation

